  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\n- In Explicit mode, a call needs a setup with a configured outcome (#428, closes #396). Verifying a void method with Called or CallCount registered a bare setup, and that setup allowed its calls, so verification switched strictness off for the arguments it matched. The same held for a property or indexer Setter(...) that was only selected or verified. Now only Returns, ReturnsAsync, Throws, ThrowsAsync, UseBaseImplementation, or Callback on a void method allows a call; a setter counts once it has a Callback or UseBaseImplementation. Implicit mode is unchanged.\n\n  Behaviour change: code that relied on a bare void setup or a bare Setter(...) to allow calls in Explicit mode now gets MissingImposterException. Configure an empty callback instead, for example imposter.Log(Arg<int>.Any()).Callback(_ => { });.\n\n  In Implicit mode, a verification-only setup of a generic method for a compatible type argument, such as AddItem<object>(Arg<object>.Any()).Called(...), no longer catches later AddItem<string> calls. They are recorded under string, as they are when no setup exists.",
